      "sample_index": 0,
      "text": "To find the value of \\( b \\) such that the equations \\( 2x + 7 = 3 \\) and \\( bx - 10 = -2 \\) have the same solution \\( x \\), we first need to solve the first equation for \\( x \\).\n\nStarting with the equation \\( 2x + 7 = 3 \\):\n1. Subtract 7 from both sides:\n\\[ 2x + 7 - 7 = 3 - 7 \\]\n\\[ 2x = -4 \\]\n2. Divide both sides by 2:\n\\[ x = \\frac{-4}{2} \\]\n\\[ x = -2 \\]\n\nNow that we have \\( x = -2 \\), we substitute this value into the second equation \\( bx - 10 = -2 \\):\n\n3. Substitute \\( x = -2 \\):\n\\[ b(-2) - 10 = -2 \\]\n4. Simplify the left side:\n\\[ -2b - 10 = -2 \\]\n5. Add 10 to both sides to isolate the term involving \\( b \\):\n\\[ -2b - 10 + 10 = -2 + 10 \\]\n\\[ -2b = 8 \\]\n6. Divide both sides by -2 to solve for \\( b \\):\n\\[ b = \\frac{8}{-2} \\]\n\\[ b = -4 \\]\n\nSo, the value of \\( b \\) is \\(\\boxed{-4}\\).",
